<p>My original draft for this article actually did that! The first version was going heavier on the &quot;meta&quot; concept, and the implication that you (the reader) are the one in the simulation. Had hidden messages and all sorts, from a doomsday group that wanted to wake up all the candidates prematurely and end the universe.</p>
<p>At the end, one would attempt to interact with you through a terminal interface and you could respond to it. However, regardless of your response, the Foundation would cut you off and redirect you to another page, falsely claiming there was a &quot;virus&quot; on the page and so it had been deleted.</p>
<p>You can find that original version here if you're curious: <a href="http://firedawnfolder.wikidot.com/fragment:scp-wakeup-0">http://firedawnfolder.wikidot.com/fragment:scp-wakeup-0</a></p>
<p>If you go to the bottom, open the last collapsible (+ Open /0/union.txt) and click one of the buttons at the bottom, it'll do the cut-out thing you expected!</p>

							</div>

								
					
